{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-18T07:42:54.124Z","data":{"text":"Done. Both gates pass.\n\n**Changed**\n- `src/core/run/verify-diff.ts` (new): `prepareVerifyDiff(projectRoot, changeFolder, config)` returns `{ path, cleanup } | null`, reading `<changeFolder>/.run/base` and writing `vcs.patch(base)` into a `fs.mkdtemp` folder under `os.tmpdir()`; missing/blank marker, `NoVcs`, and a failing patch all return null. Also exports `prepareVerifyEnv`, which builds the role env, applies `OSQ_CHANGE`/`OSQ_DIFF`, and sets `extraEnv` last.\n- `src/core/run/verification.ts`: `runVerificationCommand` now builds env + cleanup through `prepareVerifyEnv` and runs `await cleanup()` after the child, on every outcome. Signature and callers unchanged; 70 lines.\n- `tests/verify-diff.test.ts` (new): proves watcher-and-harness \"Verify gets the change's diff\" and one case per row of \"No diff without a base\", using temporary git repos and a `withEnv` probe setting `OSQ_DIFF=/stale.diff`.\n\n**Verification**\n- Task verify: 8 pass / 0 fail.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify`: exit 0 (typechecks, build, 4288 + 233 tests, lint).\n- Function/line budgets and `tests/verify-role-env.test.ts` unchanged: green.\n\nTwo notes for the planner, recorded in the result file: `verify-diff.ts` exports the env-assembly helper the acceptance allows moving there, and `node --test <missing file>` reports success on this Node version, so the declared red start was not observable."}}
